C. For contrast: classes randomized whole (cluster RCT), m=25, DE = 1+(m-1)ICC
   ICC=0.05 DE=2.20: d=0.3: 401 students = 17 classes; d=0.4: 234 students = 10 classes; d=0.5: 154 students = 7 classes
   ICC=0.1 DE=3.40: d=0.3: 619 students = 25 classes; d=0.4: 361 students = 15 classes; d=0.5: 239 students = 10 classes
   ICC=0.2 DE=5.80: d=0.3: 1056 students = 43 classes; d=0.4: 615 students = 25 classes; d=0.5: 407 students = 17 classes

D. Within-subject (each student both conditions), paired t on condition difference
   d is on the between-student SD scale; d_z = d / sqrt(2(1-rho)); rho = corr of a student's two condition scores
   rho=0.5: d=0.3 (d_z=0.30): N=90; d=0.4 (d_z=0.40): N=52; d=0.5 (d_z=0.50): N=34
   rho=0.7: d=0.3 (d_z=0.39): N=55; d=0.4 (d_z=0.52): N=32; d=0.5 (d_z=0.65): N=21

E. What 2-4 classes give: enrolled -> analysable (consent x completion, assumption)
   2 classes x 20 = 40 enrolled -> analysable at 60/70/80%: [24, 28, 32]
   2 classes x 25 = 50 enrolled -> analysable at 60/70/80%: [30, 35, 40]
   3 classes x 20 = 60 enrolled -> analysable at 60/70/80%: [36, 42, 48]
   3 classes x 25 = 75 enrolled -> analysable at 60/70/80%: [45, 52, 60]
   4 classes x 20 = 80 enrolled -> analysable at 60/70/80%: [48, 56, 64]
   4 classes x 25 = 100 enrolled -> analysable at 60/70/80%: [60, 70, 80]

